A||||7||Andy||Temperature gauge freaking out
Z||000000||Andy||07-16-99||05:31 PM||||The other day I noticed my temp.gauge jumping back and for between 100 and 160.It been doing fine,it's normal reading is about 150.Today,going to work,I noticed it never getting over 120 ,seemed stuck.The engine didn't seem any hotter.When I got back in the car I noticed the temp gauge was stuck on the very top,way past 260.It stayed there all the way home and it's still there.Wondering if I need a new gauge or what.<br>                           Andy
Z||000001||batboy||07-16-99||08:02 PM||||I'd try replacing the sensor on the engine first. Cheaper and easier. Maybe you'll luck out and that'll be the problem.
Z||000002||Taijiguy||07-31-99||02:25 PM||||You didn't mention if it actually had wa-wa in it. I had an 84 that would send the guage into major spasms if it got a little low on coolant. If not, then it probably is the sending unit. Good luck.....
Z||000003||Andy||08-02-99||02:19 PM||||Will check my coolant tommorrw ,before I get started  rewiring the tempgauge.Sofar I changed my sensor.I done the grounding trick and my needel did what it was suppose to do.It peeged out ,but then it got stuck on top again.After it got stuck the first time,it came down 2 days later by it self.Heck if I know,so I gess I will rewire it tomorrow unless anybody has any more ideas  on what else I can try.Thanks for the help<br>andy
Z||000004||batboy||08-02-99||06:38 PM||||If grounding the wire caused the needle to peg, then the wire is probably ok. If the needle pegged and then stuck, that sound to me like the gauge itself is messed up.
Z||000005||Andy||08-03-99||11:44 AM||||I just finished rewiring the temp gauge ,checked the coolant[freezepoint is -10,boiling point is 260]done the grounding trick. everything checked out.I will take it for a spin in a while, when thinks cool down and I can put everything back together.If all fells and it is my temp gauge,how in the world do I get to it wihout messing anything up in the IP Cluster.I know of a Junkyard who has an 87[same as mine,but not a gt]with the IP Cluster in it.Everything matches,except for the odometer reading,which is about69000,mine is 89000.Wouldn't it be easier to just exchange the to clusters and run the odometer up to match mine?Or do Ineed to exchange the odometers,assuming I can switch the two clusters.              Andy<br>             andy
Z||000006||DJRice||08-03-99||03:01 PM||||The temperature and fuel gauges will pop right out of the donor instrument panel and pop right into your original.  You wont need to mess with the odometer at all.  It will take you longer to get the cluster out of the car than it will to do the gauge swap.
Z||000007||batboy||08-03-99||06:11 PM||||I dreaded taking my instrument cluster out the first time, but after doing it several times, it's really not all that hard. It may be possible that you can get to the temp/gas gauges without removing the whole cluster. Try removing the big curved plastic trim under the steering wheel, then take off the silver plastic trim on the front of the instrument cluster, then the clear plastic, then the metal cover. The temp/gas gauge unit is held on with two hex head screws, remove these and pull the unit straight out (it clips into place in the back).
